import{_ as t,o,c as a,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-048 — /missions: one agency palette, era tiles with photos and agency dots, agency chips with dots and counts, a redesigned card","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-048-missions-one-agency-palette-era-tiles-with-photos-and-agency-dots.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-048-missions-one-agency-palette-era-tiles-with-photos-and-agency-dots.md"}'),n={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-048-missions-one-agency-palette-era-tiles-with-photos-and-agency-dots.md"};function r(i,e,d,c,h,l){return o(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="uxd-048-—-missions-one-agency-palette-era-tiles-with-photos-and-agency-dots-agency-chips-with-dots-and-counts-a-redesigned-card" tabindex="-1">UXD-048 — /missions: one agency palette, era tiles with photos and agency dots, agency chips with dots and counts, a redesigned card <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-048-—-missions-one-agency-palette-era-tiles-with-photos-and-agency-dots-agency-chips-with-dots-and-counts-a-redesigned-card" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-048 — /missions: one agency palette, era tiles with photos and agency dots, agency chips with dots and counts, a redesigned card&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted (built; unit tests and e2e green, see Verification; the prerender build and the full preflight were not run)</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-15</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator, 2026-11-15 — D7 &quot;in code, free route&quot;, strip option A, palette 10b, then the mission-control mock-up variant 2 (era photos, agency dots, redesigned cards)</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: MI2, MI3, D7, L50 (E3)</li><li><strong>Builds on</strong>: <a href="./UXD-014-one-chip-and-filter">UXD-014</a> (the one chip), Design System §2.4, §5.4, §5.7a</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>EntityCard</code>, <code>AgencyFilterRow</code>, <code>BrowseToolbar</code>, <code>EntityList</code>, <code>entity-card-grid.css</code>, <code>entity-browse-page.css</code>, <code>/fleet</code> page, <code>epoch-bands.ts</code> (bucketing), <code>agencyDataColor</code>, <code>src/lib/agencies.ts</code> (14 colours), <code>EpochTimelineStrip.svelte</code>, <code>Chip.svelte</code> (<code>dotColor</code>), <code>chip.css</code>, <code>era-flagships.ts</code>, <code>src/routes/missions/+page.svelte</code>, <code>MissionPanel.svelte</code> (agency row colour), <code>messages/*.json</code> (<code>missions_showing</code>), tests</li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The brief (<code>docs/wip/2026-11-13-slice-E3-brief.md</code>) counted three agency palettes, 7 of 13 agency colours under 3:1 on the page, and an era strip whose labels clipped (three of nine at 1356 px, ten at 724 px). Two prototype sheets on the real index (<code>docs/wip/2026-11-15-E3-prototypes.md</code>) measured options A (tiles), B (dot ruler) and C (repaired axis): only A kept every label inside its box in en, de and ar at 1440, 768 and 390.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>One palette for the 14 agencies on /missions</strong> (<code>agencies.ts</code> <code>color</code>): a card&#39;s accent and agency bar, the filter dot and the era tiles&#39; dots read the same value. Each is 4.5:1 or better on the page and the card, none is cyan or teal, every pair is told apart under protan, deutan and tritan simulation (CIEDE2000 above 5, neighbours in the filter row 7 or more). The badge fill is gone from the card (a bar and the agency name replace it), so no badge text colour is needed there; the panel&#39;s agency row still picks white or dark text by contrast, now 4.5:1 or better for all 14.</li><li><strong>The era strip is nine equal tiles</strong> on <code>ChipGroup role=&quot;radiogroup&quot;</code> and <code>Chip kind=&quot;choice&quot;</code>: roving focus, arrow keys, Home and End, reversed in right-to-left, the order mirrored in Arabic, year ranges isolated (<code>bdi dir=&quot;ltr&quot;</code>). A tile is the era&#39;s flagship mission hero under a dark gradient with name, years, count and one dot per active agency (at most 7, then &quot;+N&quot;). The chosen tile has the #889fe7 edge. Nine columns from a 1100 px strip, five and four below, one scroll row under 560 px.</li><li><strong>Era photos are fixed picks</strong> (<code>src/lib/era-flagships.ts</code>), the hero of one shipped mission each, never a new image: first-steps <code>sputnik1</code>, space-race <code>gemini4</code>, lunar-era <code>apollo17</code>, first-stations <code>skylab-2</code>, shuttle-and-mir <code>sts-1</code> (no mission of the index in 1987 to 1998 shows the Shuttle; STS-1 is the nearest picture of the subject and sits in the first-stations years), iss-assembly <code>spirit</code>, commercial-era <code>inspiration4</code>, lunar-return <code>artemis2</code>, mars-era <code>starship-mars-crew</code> (a computer render, credited as one). Credits are those of the hero in <code>image-provenance.json</code>.</li><li><strong>The strip and the agency row are always visible</strong>; FILTERS keeps destination, status and crew. Agency chips carry a 10 px palette dot (<code>Chip</code> <code>dotColor</code>, no ring, the selected edge stays the accent) and the mission count. A line under the filters reads the catalogue total and &quot;<code>Showing: &lt;era&gt; (&lt;n&gt;)</code>&quot;.</li><li><strong>The card</strong>: photo, name with the year at the row&#39;s end, one line per agency (3 px bar in its colour, then the name), status pill, the story.</li></ol><h2 id="amendment-round-2-2026-11-15-one-pattern-for-missions-and-fleet" tabindex="-1">Amendment, round 2 (2026-11-15): one pattern for /missions and /fleet <a class="header-anchor" href="#amendment-round-2-2026-11-15-one-pattern-for-missions-and-fleet" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Amendment, round 2 (2026-11-15): one pattern for /missions and /fleet&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The operator: cards &quot;have to stay the same size they were&quot;; &quot;missions and fleet are two sides of the same coin&quot;. The card, the grid, the agency row, the toolbar and the list became shared components, and /fleet was brought into line. The pages that use the card and the grid are /missions and /fleet only.</p><ol><li><strong>One card, one footprint</strong> (<code>EntityCard</code>, <code>entity-card-grid.css</code>): photo plus a fixed 142 px body of four rows, so no card has an empty band or stretches past its row. Card heights, first 16 cards, before E3 (<code>eadf9e3978a^</code>) and now: /missions 277 to 285 px at 1440, 302 to 330 at 768, 252 to 289 at 390, now 287, 340 and 241; /fleet 326 to 381, 347 to 418 and 278 to 404, now 287, 340 and 241. One height per width on both pages, within 2 px of the old /missions card and 40 to 100 px shorter than the old /fleet card; the empty band under the last row is 37 px at most (a record without a story).</li><li><strong>Black photos</strong>: the cause is not a missing image. The first card image gets its <code>src</code> only when the image-ladder manifest and the hero overrides have loaded (<code>responsive()</code> returns no <code>src</code> after mount until then; a log of one cold load: first card image in the DOM at 4.45 s, the manifest at 4.34 s, painted at 4.55 s), and until then the slot showed the 40 % black fill. The slot is now the soft gradient. Screenshots wait for the images.</li><li><strong>Agency chips</strong> show the name, the dot and the count; the logos are dropped (dark on dark).</li><li><strong>Era photos</strong>: Shuttle &amp; Mir is STS-1 (the Columbia launch); it was counted in First Stations because the bands overlap and the earlier band won; where bands share more than a boundary year the later band now wins (1981 to 1986 move to Shuttle &amp; Mir: 12 and 15 missions). Mars Era shows Perseverance on Mars (a photo) instead of the Starship render. Text over every tile photo is at least 6.6:1 (sampled: the brightest pixel under each text box).</li><li><strong>Sort and Grid / List</strong> exist on both pages (/fleet had sort in its filters and a list view by URL only); they are in the toolbar.</li><li><strong>Differences found and how they were resolved</strong>: strip inside FILTERS on /fleet, always visible on /missions → visible on both; agency chips inside FILTERS with logos on both → one visible row, names; sort only on /fleet → toolbar on both; view toggle in the filters row on /fleet, none on /missions → toolbar; &quot;Showing&quot; line only on /missions → both; CLEAR FILTERS only while the filters were open → whenever a filter is on; two card layouts (badge, type, country on /fleet; badge, type, destination on /missions) → one card, country and destination are hidden facts, the category is a pill; content-visibility only on /fleet → the grid; page padding 22 px vs 12 px on a phone and a smaller card name on /fleet → one frame (<code>.browse-main</code>) and one name size; /fleet agency dots use brand colours lifted to 4.5:1 where the palette has no value. Kept per type: the FILTERS chip disabled in the line-up, the Line-up view, the category filter, the destination and crew filters, the launches banner, how the era counts are made (year bands vs the entry&#39;s epoch).</li></ol><h2 id="amendment-round-3-2026-11-15-the-photo-sits-on-the-right-the-text-on-plain-dark" tabindex="-1">Amendment, round 3 (2026-11-15): the photo sits on the right, the text on plain dark <a class="header-anchor" href="#amendment-round-3-2026-11-15-the-photo-sits-on-the-right-the-text-on-plain-dark" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Amendment, round 3 (2026-11-15): the photo sits on the right, the text on plain dark&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The operator: the photos were &quot;very murky&quot; under the gradient, &quot;not as good as in the idea&quot; (the mock-up). The tile is now the mock-up&#39;s layout: the text column on the tile&#39;s dark surface at the start, the photo crisp and at full brightness on the end side (40 % of the tile, the square crop, a per-era object position, a short fade at its inner edge); selected tile #889fe7. Text contrast no longer depends on the photo (12.2:1 at the worst text box, measured on the dark area, /missions and /fleet, 1440 and 390 px; before it was 4.23 at the worst tile). Agency dots: at most 5. The flagship picks were reviewed for a subject that reads at about 60 px: first-steps <code>sputnik1</code>, space-race <code>gemini4</code>, lunar-era <code>apollo17</code> (unchanged); first-stations <code>skylab-2</code> → <code>skylab-4</code> (slot 04, NASA, &quot;View of Skylab space station cluster in Earth orbit&quot;, PD-NASA); shuttle-and-mir <code>sts-1</code> (unchanged); iss-assembly <code>spirit</code> → <code>curiosity</code> (PIA16239 self-portrait, NASA/JPL, PD-NASA); commercial-era <code>inspiration4</code> → <code>chandrayaan3</code> (LVM3 M4 lifting off, ISRO, PD-self); lunar-return <code>artemis2</code> (unchanged); mars-era <code>perseverance</code> → <code>spirit</code> (a real photograph of a Mars rover, NASA, PD-NASA, KSC-03PD-0784).</p><h2 id="amendment-round-4-2026-11-15-programs-and-missions-launches-on-the-pattern" tabindex="-1">Amendment, round 4 (2026-11-15): /programs and /missions/launches on the pattern <a class="header-anchor" href="#amendment-round-4-2026-11-15-programs-and-missions-launches-on-the-pattern" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Amendment, round 4 (2026-11-15): /programs and /missions/launches on the pattern&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The operator approved /missions + /fleet as one pattern and said &quot;we can do the others&quot;.</p><ol><li><strong>/programs</strong>. Differences found and resolved: groups under headings by era, kind or agency (state only) → the era strip, the agency chips and a kind filter in FILTERS; no search, sort or list → search, the toolbar with sort and Grid / List; its own 300 px anchor card of varying height (349 to 472 px at 1440) → <code>EntityCard</code> as a link, one size (287, 341 and 236 px at 1440, 768 and 390); oldest first inside groups → newest first by default, <code>?sort=chrono-asc</code>. <strong>Era rule</strong>: a program belongs to the era of its start year, by <code>epochForYear</code> (the rule /missions applies to a mission&#39;s year); the program&#39;s own <code>epoch</code> label disagrees with its dates for 19 of 42 programs and is not used. Era counts 5, 4, 2, 5, 9, 9, 6, 2, 0. Kept: the title, lead and patch wall (an editorial index; the frame is the wide page shell, <code>page-shell.spec</code>), the program page it links to. New params: <code>epoch</code>, <code>agency</code>, <code>kind</code>, <code>q</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>view</code> (there were none).</li><li><strong>/missions/launches</strong>. Differences found and resolved: the agency as a searchable dropdown inside FILTERS → the provider chips by short name (<code>?agency=</code> still accepts the manifest&#39;s full names); CLEAR inside the panel and only for four filters → CLEAR FILTERS in the bar for every filter including era and search; no era strip, search, sort or grid → added; one frame of its own (1400 px, 22 px) → <code>.browse-main</code>. <strong>List stays the month-grouped <code>LaunchRow</code> list and is the default</strong> (the manifest is long; the rows carry the countdown, provenance, editorial note and links, which <code>EntityList</code> has no column for); <code>?view=grid</code> is one <code>EntityCard</code> per launch. The page holds one manifest at a time (upcoming, or one decade), so the era tiles count from <code>static/data/launches-years.json</code> (launches per year and provider, written by <code>fetch-launches.ts</code>, guarded by a unit test) and <strong>choosing an era loads the decades it spans</strong> (and the upcoming list when the era runs to the present) and keeps the launches of its years; the view and decade chips step aside while an era is on. Kept and proved by <code>catalogue-pattern-programs-launches.spec.ts</code>: <code>mode</code>, <code>decade</code>, <code>tier</code>, <code>agency</code>, <code>outcome</code>, <code>year</code> (the FILTERS panel still opens when a URL carries one of them except agency). New: <code>epoch</code>, <code>q</code>, <code>sort</code> (oldest first, soonest first when upcoming, is the default), <code>view</code>.</li><li><strong>Pills</strong>. The kind of a program is the first pill and shows whole (the singular <code>program_kind_*</code> form, tighter tracking); the status gives way to it and is hidden on the two-column phone grid (the years already say ongoing or ended; it stays in the hidden facts). A launch&#39;s tier pill is hidden on that grid. Joint programs list their agencies without squeezing into each other.</li><li><strong>Mars Era on /programs counts 0</strong>: the strip is shared and shows an empty era with its 0 (as /missions would), not hidden and not dimmed.</li></ol><h2 id="amendment-round-3b-2026-11-16-a-long-fade-three-new-photos-empty-eras-dimmed" tabindex="-1">Amendment, round 3b (2026-11-16): a long fade, three new photos, empty eras dimmed <a class="header-anchor" href="#amendment-round-3b-2026-11-16-a-long-fade-three-new-photos-empty-eras-dimmed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Amendment, round 3b (2026-11-16): a long fade, three new photos, empty eras dimmed&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The operator: &quot;still not good&quot;, the photos read as a thin strip. The photo now spans the end 70 % of the tile (a square crop) with a long ease-in fade from 30 % to 60 % of the tile, near-transparent under the text; the name wraps within 59 % of the text box; the years are 90 % white. Contrast (brightest pixel under each text box, 1440 and 390 px, /missions and /fleet): 5.49 at worst. <code>era-flagships.ts</code> is now <code>ERA_PHOTO</code> (folder, id, slot, object position, <code>flipRtl</code>); the tile draws <code>&lt;slot&gt;.1x1.jpg</code>, which <code>era-flagships.test.ts</code> requires to exist. The Sputnik crop is mirrored in right-to-left, where its subject would land in the fade. Picks, old → new: iss-assembly <code>curiosity</code> → the ISS after STS-132 undocking (<code>fleet-galleries/iss</code> slot 03; NASA, STS-132 crew, PD-NASA); lunar-return <code>artemis2</code> → the Artemis I rollout, SLS at night (<code>missions/artemis1</code> slot 02; NASA/Isaac Watson, PD-NASA); mars-era <code>spirit</code> → a real Starship launch photo, &quot;SpaceX Starship ignition during IFT-5&quot; (<code>fleet-galleries/starship</code> slot 01; Steve Jurvetson, CC-BY-2.0, credited on /credits with the gallery); the others are kept (sputnik1, gemini4, apollo17, skylab-4 slot 04, sts-1, chandrayaan3 slot 03). An era with no entries on a page stays in the strip, dimmed and not selectable (Mars Era on /programs): <code>aria-disabled</code>, skipped by arrow keys, no hover lift, its count reads 0; one already chosen stays selectable (<code>eraSelectable</code>); <code>tests/e2e/era-strip-empty.spec.ts</code>.</p><h2 id="amendment-round-5-2026-11-16-each-photo-placed-by-hand-a-real-gradient-the-review-leftovers" tabindex="-1">Amendment, round 5 (2026-11-16): each photo placed by hand, a real gradient, the review leftovers <a class="header-anchor" href="#amendment-round-5-2026-11-16-each-photo-placed-by-hand-a-real-gradient-the-review-leftovers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Amendment, round 5 (2026-11-16): each photo placed by hand, a real gradient, the review leftovers&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The operator: still black under the letters, the subjects small and in the middle, &quot;do a normal gradient&quot;, &quot;image recognize each card&quot;. Round 3b&#39;s square crop and fade are replaced (<code>edc893238da</code>):</p><ol><li><strong>Placement per photo.</strong> <code>ERA_PHOTO</code> gives each era its rung (<code>-640</code>, or <code>-1280</code> for ISS and Artemis I), aspect, subject focus point and drawn height, read from a gridded sheet of the nine sources; <code>eraPhotoPlacement</code> puts the focus at 72 % of the tile (28 % in right-to-left) and the picture always covers the tile&#39;s full height (<code>era-flagships.test.ts</code>, which caught a 3 px gap on the ISS). Each photo fades in at its own edge, so a narrow tile has no seam. The subjects: Sputnik whole, the spacewalker, the astronaut by the rover, Skylab, the Shuttle on the pad, the ISS over Earth, LVM3 lifting off, SLS at night, Starship igniting.</li><li><strong>Gradient.</strong> The photo is under the whole tile; over it the dark surface runs from solid at the text edge, thinning through 55 %, clear from 70 % (78 % on the phone). No hard block.</li><li><strong>Text.</strong> The name keeps whole words (<code>keep-all</code>: &quot;COMMERCIAL&quot; no longer splits) within 52 %; at most three agency dots, then &quot;+N&quot;, and the count row stays within 58 % so it never reaches the photo (it did on <code>/fleet</code>). Phone tiles are 172 px (were 132).</li><li><strong>Review leftovers</strong> (<code>92f051b7be6</code>): First Stations is <strong>1973-1980</strong>: 1981-1986 were already counted under Shuttle &amp; Mir, so the label said more than the tile counted; the bands no longer overlap. The agency row&#39;s &quot;Show all 44&quot; has &quot;Show fewer&quot; (<code>browse_show_fewer</code>, 14 locales). A <code>/programs</code> card has one pill, the kind, whole in every language; the name takes up to two lines and the tagline one; the status pill is gone from the card (the years say running or ended; the status is in the list and read out). On the phone grid the years go under the name. A <code>/fleet</code> card for hardware that has not flown shows no year; its PLANNED pill says it.</li></ol><p>Checked tile by tile at 1440 and 390 px on <code>/missions</code> (en, ar) and <code>/fleet</code>; <code>catalogue-pattern.spec.ts</code> gained the Show all / Show fewer case.</p><h2 id="not-changed-on-purpose" tabindex="-1">Not changed on purpose <a class="header-anchor" href="#not-changed-on-purpose" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Not changed on purpose&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The mission <code>color</code> in the data files stays (explore&#39;s paths, the HUD rings and the overlay accent read it; 11 of the 139 differ from the registry). <code>/missions</code> reads the registry.</li><li>The chip colours of <code>nation-palette.ts</code> and the other 23 agencies&#39; brand colours.</li></ul><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>agency-palette.test.ts</code> (contrast, colour-blind distance, distinctness over the index&#39;s agencies), <code>epoch-bands.test.ts</code> (era bucketing and totals), <code>era-flagships.test.ts</code> (nine picks, hero files exist), <code>tests/e2e/missions-era-strip.spec.ts</code> and <code>missions-filters-cards.spec.ts</code> on desktop-chromium and mobile-chromium against the dev server.</p>',24)])])}const u=t(n,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,u as default};
